On the 28 October 2024, the dataset was extended to cover the period of 2022 until June 2024 (satellites Metop-B, Metop-C, NOAA-15, NOAA-18, NOAA-19). Note that as part of this extension, the entire Metop-C record was reprocessed with improved calibration coefficients from PATMOS-X.","identifier":"EO:EUM:DAT:0862","name":"AVHRR Fundamental Data Record - Release 1 - Multimission"}

{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"Dataset","url":"https://navigator.eumetsat.int/product/EO:EUM:DAT:0590","measurementTechnique":"Interferometer","copyrightHolder":{"@type":"Organization","name":"EUMETSAT","contactPoint":{"@type":"ContactPoint","contactType":"customer support","email":"ops@eumetsat.int","url":"https://user.eumetsat.int"}},"copyrightYear":"2007","creator":{"@type":"Organization","name":"EUMETSAT","contactPoint":{"@type":"ContactPoint","contactType":"customer support","email":"ops@eumetsat.int","url":"https://user.eumetsat.int"}},"dateCreated":"Wed Jan 10 00:07:00 UTC 2007","isAccessibleForFree":"false","keywords":"GEO,Metop,EPS Native,Climate,Numerical weather prediction,Interferometer,NWP-based reanalysis,IASI","license":"https://eoportal.eumetsat.int/userMgmt/terms.faces","publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"EUMETSAT","contactPoint":{"@type":"ContactPoint","contactType":"customer support","email":"ops@eumetsat.int","url":"https://user.eumetsat.int"}},"schemaVersion":"3.5","spatialCoverage":{"@type":"Place","geo":{"@type":"GeoShape","polygon":"-180.0  90.0  180.0  -90.0"}},"temporalCoverage":"Wed Jan 10 00:07:00 UTC 2007 / Wed Jan 30 00:09:00 UTC 2019","thumbnailUrl":"https://user.eumetsat.int/s3/eup-strapi-media/iasi_91e9304add.jpg","encodingFormat":"EPS Native","description":"The main objective of the Infrared Atmospheric Sounding Interferometer (IASI) is to provide high-resolution atmospheric emission spectra to derive temperature and humidity profiles with high spectral and vertical resolution and accuracy. Additionally it is used for the determination of trace gases such as ozone, nitrous oxide, carbon dioxide and methane, as well as land and sea surface temperature, emissivity and cloud properties.

The IASI level 1c product contains infrared radiance spectra at 0.25cm-1 resolution. The product has for each sounded pixel 8461 spectral samples covering the range between 645.0 cm-1 and 2760 cm-1 wavenumbers.

This is the Metop-A and -B IASI L1c Release 2 data record. It corrects a residual non-linearity error of the order 0.1-0.2 K in the long wave part of the spectra thus improving the time and inter-instrument radiance consistencies. This release comprises L1c data from Metop-A and -B satellites for the period ranging from the 10th of July 2007 until the 30th of September 2019. This is a Fundamental Climate Data Record (FCDR), , ie, a long-term data record of calibrated and quality-controlled sensor data designed to allow the generation of homogeneous products that are accurate and stable enough for climate monitoring and data assimilation for re-analysis of the recent climate.","identifier":"EO:EUM:DAT:0590","name":"IASI Level 1C Climate Data Record Release 2 - Metop-A and -B"}

{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"Dataset","url":"https://navigator.eumetsat.int/product/EO:EUM:DAT:0442","measurementTechnique":"Interferometer","copyrightHolder":{"@type":"Organization","name":"EUMETSAT","contactPoint":{"@type":"ContactPoint","contactType":"customer support","email":"ops@eumetsat.int","url":"https://user.eumetsat.int"}},"copyrightYear":"2026","creator":{"@type":"Organization","name":"EUMETSAT","contactPoint":{"@type":"ContactPoint","contactType":"customer support","email":"ops@eumetsat.int","url":"https://user.eumetsat.int"}},"dateCreated":"Wed Jan 07 00:10:00 UTC 2026","isAccessibleForFree":"false","keywords":"GEO,Weather,Climate,Atmospheric composition,Metop-SG,Interferometer,netCDF4,IASI-NG","license":"https://eoportal.eumetsat.int/userMgmt/terms.faces","publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"EUMETSAT","contactPoint":{"@type":"ContactPoint","contactType":"customer support","email":"ops@eumetsat.int","url":"https://user.eumetsat.int"}},"schemaVersion":"3.5","spatialCoverage":{"@type":"Place","geo":{"@type":"GeoShape","polygon":"-180.0  90.0  180.0  -90.0"}},"temporalCoverage":"Wed Jan 07 00:10:00 UTC 2026 / Fri Nov 13 00:14:52 UTC 2026","thumbnailUrl":"https://user.eumetsat.int/s3/eup-strapi-media/placeholder_dd19f07bd6.png","encodingFormat":"netCDF4","description":"IASI-NG, a passive infrared sounder, measures temperature and water vapour profiles of the Earth’s atmosphere. IASI-NG also has a huge potential to measure greenhouse gases, clouds, aerosols, ozone, and trace gases.

