High Resolution Layer Tree Cover and Forest product is part of the European Union’s Copernicus Land Monitoring Service.","identifier":"EO:CLMS:DAT:TCD_100M_YEARLY_2018_PRESENT","name":"Tree Cover Density 2018 - Present (raster 100m), Europe, yearly, Nov. 2024"}

{"@context":"http://schema.org/","@type":"Dataset","url":"https://navigator.eumetsat.int/product/EO:CLMS:DAT:SWI_12_5KM_DAILY_V4","copyrightYear":"2007","dateCreated":"Wed Jan 10 00:01:00 UTC 2007","datePublished":"Tue Jan 14 00:11:00 UTC 2025","isAccessibleForFree":"false","keywords":"biogeophysical,soil moisture,daily composite,global,World,Global,Daily,NetCDF,Soil,Agriculture and food,Orthoimagery,soil water index,geophysical environment","schemaVersion":"3.5","spatialCoverage":{"@type":"Place","geo":{"@type":"GeoShape","polygon":"-180.0  90.0  180.0  -90.0"}},"temporalCoverage":"Wed Jan 10 00:01:00 UTC 2007 / Thu Sep 17 15:49:56 UTC 2026","thumbnailUrl":"https://sdi.eea.europa.eu/catalogue/api/records/7417c491-9706-4eb4-989c-e339b27b1bc5/attachments/SWI12.5km-V4_thumbnail.png","encodingFormat":"NetCDF","description":"The Soil Water index (SWI) product provides global daily information about moisture conditions in different soil layers. SWI daily images are produced from EUMETSAT ASCAT-25km SSM product in orbit format and include a quality flag indicating the availability of SSM measurements for SWI calculations. Soil moisture is a key parameter in numerous environmental studies including hydrology, meteorology and agriculture. In addition to Surface Soil Moisture (SSM), information on the moisture condition within the underlying soil profile is of interest for different applications. 

